14m7|v|To cut into long slices or strips and dry in the sun; as, jerk beef. See Charqui. ; To beat; to strike. ; To give a quick and suddenly arrested thrust, push, pull, or twist, to; to yerk; as, to jerk one with the elbow; to jerk a coat off. ; To throw with a quick and suddenly arrested motion of the hand; as, to jerk a stone. ; To make a sudden motion; to move with a start, or by starts. ; To flout with contempt.	o:175i,34,1;fq4,28,2~fq4,28,2;175i,34,1
